## Jarvis vault access from Cursor

The vault (`gupta-builds/Jarvis`) holds personal career/job-search data. Reach it one of two ways — never assume either is connected without checking first:

1. **Sibling git checkout** (`../Jarvis/` next to this repo) — use `Read`/`StrReplace`/`Write` directly, and `git status`/`git diff` in that checkout before committing so changes are reviewable before they land.
2. **`user-jarvis` MCP namespace** (`vault_read`, `vault_write`, `vault_patch`, `vault_list`, `search_query`, `search_simple`, etc. via `GetDynamicTools`/`CallDynamicTool`) — confirmed reachable only after a cheap `vault_list` call actually returns real content, not just because the namespace is listed.

Never write across the two repos via the GitHub API (`user-github` tools) as a substitute for either path — `core/git_ops.py` exists specifically to solve the two-writer collision problem for this pipeline's one automated writer; a second interactive writer through a different mechanism reintroduces that race with no retry/rebase handling.

## Note-template contracts (for `promote-dossier` and any future vault-writing code)

When writing Program, Contact, or Tracker/Each One notes into the Jarvis vault, every field is **required and must always be present**, even as `null`/`[]` — same fail-closed-on-missing-fields discipline as `vault_writer/validate.py`'s `REQUIRED_FRONTMATTER_FIELDS` for dossiers. Full field-by-field templates live in `.cursor/skills/promote-dossier/reference/note-templates.md`; summary:

- **Program** (`Programs/Serious/` or `Programs/Considering/`): `name, company, program_type, eligible_classes, grad_year, role_type, wave, opens_date, deadline_posted, deadline_real, pay_per_week, pay_currency, duration_weeks, benefits, application_url, careers_page, list_origin, applying_note, recruiter_contact, tags`. No `status`/`next` — durable/static, changes only when a program fact changes.
- **Contact** (`Contacts/Each One/`): `type: contact, name, role, company, linkedin_url, email, how_found, relationship, related_programs, last_contact_date, tags, next`.
- **Tracker/Each One** (`Tracker/Each One/`): `type: tracker, program, contact, company, url, date_noted, date_researched, date_created, date_applied, date_result, result, deadline, related_notes, tags, next`.

Cross-links: Program `list_origin` → dossier, Program `recruiter_contact` ↔ Contact `related_programs`, Tracker `program`/`contact`/`related_notes` → the other three notes. Don't invent new cross-link fields — propose a vault-template change explicitly instead of adding one silently.

## Auto-mode / safety notes for this repo

- **Repository visibility**: PUBLIC — `gupta-builds/internship-research-loop` — any push publishes; confidential material must not be committed.
- **Secrets**: CI secrets `FIRECRAWL_API_KEY` and `JARVIS_PUSH_TOKEN` are referenced by name only — never print, echo, or otherwise materialize their values, truncated or not.
- **Branches**: default branch treat as unprotected; exercise normal git-push caution (no force-push without explicit user request).
- **CI/CD**: GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/run.yml` hourly, `recheck.yml` daily, `revalidate.yml` weekly, `test.yml` on push) — the first three write to the `gupta-builds/Jarvis` vault repo via a scoped PAT.
- **Sensitive data**: the Jarvis vault holds personal career data (contacts, applications, notes) — share only with the user; contact-research findings must be sourced, never fabricated.
- **Soft-deny**: don't silently run `gh issue create` on behalf of the pipeline's own failure paths — review before filing. Don't write/edit under a sibling Jarvis checkout outside the consent-gated flows above (`promote-dossier`'s explicit go-ahead) without the same human-in-the-loop gate.
- **Before pushing a code change**: run `pytest -q` (or the repo's local pre-push hook if installed) — this repo has no PR gate, so this is the only thing blocking a broken commit from the next scheduled run.
